          "type": "intro",
          "title": "The Constitution as Text",
          "content": "The U.S. Constitution is the supreme law of the land — a 4,543-word document ratified in 1788 that creates a government, allocates power, and protects rights. But what does it mean to 'read' the Constitution? Two camps battle over this question: originalists who seek the text's meaning in 1788, and living constitutionalists who see it as evolving with society.",
