          "type": "diagram",
          "svg": `<svg viewBox="0 0 1100 1100" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><rect width="1100" height="1100" fill="#1a1a2e"/><text x="550" y="70" font-size="36" fill="#ffd700" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="bold">Spending, Coercion, New Federalism</text><text x="550" y="115" font-size="24" fill="#888" text-anchor="middle">The map of federal leverage over states</text><rect x="80" y="160" width="940" height="150" rx="15" fill="#6366f1" opacity="0.25" stroke="#6366f1" stroke-width="3"/><text x="550" y="205" font-size="24" fill="#ffd700" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="bold">South Dakota v. Dole (1987)</text><text x="550" y="248" font-size="20" fill="#ffffff" text-anchor="middle">Conditions must be clear, related, and not coercive</text><text x="550" y="285" font-size="19" fill="#888" text-anchor="middle">5% of highway funds for a 21 drinking age = OK</text><rect x="80" y="330" width="940" height="170" rx="15" fill="#ef4444" opacity="0.25" stroke="#ef4444" stroke-width="3"/><text x="550" y="375" font-size="24" fill="#ffd700" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="bold">NFIB v. Sebelius (2012)</text><text x="550" y="418" font-size="20" fill="#ffffff" text-anchor="middle">Threatening ALL Medicaid funds = "a gun to the head"</text><text x="550" y="453" font-size="20" fill="#ffffff" text-anchor="middle">Coercion, not persuasion — expansion made optional</text><text x="550" y="488" font-size="19" fill="#f59e0b" text-anchor="middle">Dole's coercion limit finally enforced</text><rect x="80" y="520" width="220" height="220" rx="15" fill="#ef4444" opacity="0.25" stroke="#ef4444" stroke-width="2"/><text x="190" y="560" font-size="19" fill="#ffd700" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="bold">Command</text><text x="190" y="598" font-size="16" fill="#ffffff" text-anchor="middle">Order states to</text><text x="190" y="622" font-size="16" fill="#ffffff" text-anchor="middle">legislate</text><text x="190" y="668" font-size="16" fill="#ef4444" text-anchor="middle">FORBIDDEN</text><text x="190" y="702" font-size="14" fill="#888" text-anchor="middle">New York (1992)</text><rect x="320" y="520" width="220" height="220" rx="15" fill="#10b981" opacity="0.25" stroke="#10b981" stroke-width="2"/><text x="430" y="560" font-size="19" fill="#ffd700" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="bold">Preempt</text><text x="430" y="598" font-size="16" fill="#ffffff" text-anchor="middle">Regulate people;</text><text x="430" y="622" font-size="16" fill="#ffffff" text-anchor="middle">void state law</text><text x="430" y="668" font-size="16" fill="#10b981" text-anchor="middle">ALLOWED</text><text x="430" y="702" font-size="14" fill="#888" text-anchor="middle">Supremacy Clause</text><rect x="560" y="520" width="220" height="220" rx="15" fill="#10b981" opacity="0.25" stroke="#10b981" stroke-width="2"/><text x="670" y="560" font-size="19" fill="#ffd700" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="bold">Purchase</text><text x="670" y="598" font-size="16" fill="#ffffff" text-anchor="middle">Modest grant with</text><text x="670" y="622" font-size="16" fill="#ffffff" text-anchor="middle">a condition</text><text x="670" y="668" font-size="16" fill="#10b981" text-anchor="middle">ALLOWED</text><text x="670" y="702" font-size="14" fill="#888" text-anchor="middle">Dole (1987)</text><rect x="800" y="520" width="220" height="220" rx="15" fill="#ef4444" opacity="0.25" stroke="#ef4444" stroke-width="2"/><text x="910" y="560" font-size="19" fill="#ffd700" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="bold">Coerce</text><text x="910" y="598" font-size="16" fill="#ffffff" text-anchor="middle">Cut ALL funds</text><text x="910" y="622" font-size="16" fill="#ffffff" text-anchor="middle">unless complied</text><text x="910" y="668" font-size="16" fill="#ef4444" text-anchor="middle">FORBIDDEN</text><text x="910" y="702" font-size="14" fill="#888" text-anchor="middle">NFIB (2012)</text><rect x="80" y="760" width="940" height="120" rx="15" fill="#8b5cf6" opacity="0.25" stroke="#8b5cf6" stroke-width="3"/><text x="550" y="805" font-size="24" fill="#ffd700" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="bold">The New Federalism</text><text x="550" y="847" font-size="20" fill="#ffffff" text-anchor="middle">D.C. may persuade, preempt, or purchase — never command</text><rect x="80" y="900" width="940" height="120" rx="15" fill="#ffd700" opacity="0.2" stroke="#ffd700" stroke-width="3"/><text x="550" y="945" font-size="24" fill="#ffd700" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="bold">The Bottom Line</text><text x="550" y="987" font-size="20" fill="#10b981" text-anchor="middle">The Tenth Amendment: from "truism" to a patrolled border</text></svg>`,
